<Base title="About Break 90 Golf & Our Editorial Approach" description="Learn how Break 90 Golf prepares practical golf advice, research-based gear recommendations and public course guides, with clear affiliate disclosures.">
 <section class="page-heading dark-section"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow lime">ABOUT BREAK 90 GOLF</div><h1>LESS THINKING.<br/><span class="lime">BETTER GOLF.</span></h1><p>Practical golf ideas for everyday players chasing a score in the 80s.</p></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>What you will find here</h2><p>Break 90 Golf publishes scoring strategy, focused practice tasks, public golf course guides and useful equipment or book recommendations. Our <a href="/#break-90-math">breaking 90 math</a> shows how a manageable mix of pars and bogeys can add up to 89.</p><h2>How we prepare recommendations</h2><p>Course and buying guides use editorial research, including information from operators, public agencies, manufacturers, authors and publishers. We link to supporting sources where relevant. We distinguish research from firsthand experience and do not claim to have played a course, tested a product or read a book unless that experience is documented.</p><h2>Course prices and access</h2><p>Our course guides are editorial shortlists, not official statewide rankings. Rates are dated references, and we identify resident, visitor, seasonal and cart differences when the source provides them. Conditions and availability change. Confirm maintenance, the final price and cancellation terms with the operator before booking.</p><h2>Gear, books and affiliate links</h2><p>Recommendations explain a practical use, limitations and alternatives where appropriate. Some links may earn a commission. <strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong> Read our <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> for details. An affiliate link does not establish that we have tested an item or that it will improve a score.</p><h2>Original article graphics</h2><p>Our diagrams and course-planning illustrations are original educational graphics. They are not photographs of named courses or reproductions of manufacturer product images. Captions identify schematic examples and other limits.</p><h2>Start with a useful task</h2><p>Follow our <a href="/start-here/">start-here guide</a>, compare <a href="/courses/">public courses by state</a> or explore <a href="/articles/">the playbook</a>. For email updates, subscribe to <a href="/#newsletter">The Sunday Round</a>. You can unsubscribe using the link in any newsletter.</p></div></section>
</Base>
